# Observed: 3132 edits across 61 files apply cleanly with 0 conflicts, but the
# rebuild then fails with 739 stale-name errors in 16 files.
#
# History, so the trend is legible: 18081 errors in 52 files originally; 2993 in
# 36 once colliding renames were skipped; 739 in 16 once macro arguments were
# renamed and unrewritable macro references started vetoing the rename. What is
# left is a different bug, no longer anything to do with macros -- see below.
REPO=googletest
RULESET=member_snake_case
EXPECT=known_fail
EXPECT_FAIL_PHASE=rebuild
EXPECT_FAIL_REASON="Members of a class nested inside a class template: primaryTemplateMember() only maps a field back to the primary template when its parent is a ClassTemplateSpecializationDecl, but Outer<int>::Inner is an ordinary CXXRecordDecl instantiated from a member class. The key misses, so the declaration is renamed while uses are skipped -- and dependent uses are vetoed, which is where gtest-param-util.h's ValuesInIteratorRangeGenerator<T>::Iterator::iterator_ goes stale. Minimal repro: template <class T> struct Outer { struct Inner { int itemCount; }; }; int use(Outer<int>::Inner& i) { return i.itemCount; }"
